  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14239685/assets/d73138fe191ed536299fa6dca679e5948b389d26b4d9e32518eee79123f81f0e.png)\n\nGiven the diagram shown above, what is the measure of $\\overset{―}{BC}?$",
  "worked_solution": "The segments addition postulate can be applied to a set of more than three collinear points. In the given situation, it states that\n\n$$\nAD=AB+BC+CD.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the known values into the equation above, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AD & =AB+BC+CD \\\\ 28 & =9+BC+7 \\\\ 28 & =16+BC \\\\ 28-16 & =BC \\\\ BC & =12\\end{aligned}\n$$",
